WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.212
Idea. Imagine every football referee used different rules. Nobody could compare one match with another. Accountants agree on shared rules too, so accounts can be trusted and compared.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:23.683
These rules are called accounting concepts. You need six, plus going concern: accruals, business entity, consistency, materiality, money measurement, and prudence.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:39.643
Method. Learn one key idea for each. Accruals: record income and expenses in the period they belong to. Business entity: the business is separate from its owner. Consistency: use the same method every year.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:56.471
Materiality: very small items, like a stapler, can simply be treated as an expense. Money measurement: record only what has a money value. Prudence: do not overstate profit or assets. Going concern: the business will keep trading.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:08.110
In a question, find the key idea in the statement, match it to one concept, and write the name exactly. If a description is asked, explain it in your own short sentence.

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:20.395
Worked example. Here is a real question from June 2025. It gives three descriptions, and we must name the accounting concept for each. Three marks.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:29.386
Row one says low-value items do not need separate recording. The key idea is too small to matter. That is materiality.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:38.396
Row two says only items that can be measured in money are recorded. The key idea is a money value. That is money measurement.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:49.797
Row three says the business is completely separate from its owner. That is business entity. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:02:03.069
Common mistake. A common mistake is mixing up business entity and going concern. Business entity means the owner is kept separate. Going concern means the business keeps trading.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:11.584
Another is describing a concept with its own name, like consistency means being consistent. Say what it actually does.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:20.369
Your turn. Now you try. Read the three statements, and name the accounting concept for each. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:34.905
Answer. One: the holiday is kept out of the shop's books, so the owner is separate. That is business entity. Two: the same method every year is consistency. Three: the cautious figure is prudence.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:43.232
Remember: find the key idea, match it to one concept, and write its exact name. Now try the practice questions.
